# Rule: Saving Plans Locally

## Requirement

When creating a plan via CreatePlan, always specify the path to the project's local folder `.cursor/plans/`, not the global Cursor folder.

## Why This Matters

- Plans stay in the repository and are available to the whole team
- Planning history is preserved alongside the code
- Plans can be committed to git to track architectural decisions

## How to Fix

CreatePlan saves to the global folder by default. After creating a plan, always move it to the project:

- ❌ `/Users/user/.cursor/plans/plan.md` (global folder)
- ✅ `/Users/user/project/.cursor/plans/plan.md` (project local folder)

## Actions After CreatePlan

1. Read the created plan from the global folder
2. Write it to `<workspace>/.cursor/plans/<plan_name>.plan.md`
3. Remove from the global folder (optional)
